Serve static files with services.nginx (its virtualHosts.<name>.root), not with
darkhttpd: two mints in a row wired darkhttpd's listen address through an option
whose value it rejects at startup, and nginx's own module builds the config, so
there is one less hand-written argument to get wrong.

Where a unit's job is to WRITE a file before something serves it, let the
command write the file itself (a redirection inside the script it runs), rather
than routing the unit's standard output into a path: systemd opens that path
before it creates the directory the path lives in.
